    "done_when": "Following rule 1 of the block headed Retention, authorised by the lead on 2026-10-01 in section 8 of docs/plans/serving-record-warehouse.html: when the ingest offers the index a job's receipt files, the index keeps samples from exactly one tier per job, the raw file when it exists, otherwise the minute tier, otherwise the hour tier; samples already held from a job's non-selected tier are removed in the same transaction; deleting a job's raw file makes the next tick move that job to its minute tier. Tests in tests/test_telemetry_index.py over a fixture receipts directory assert that a window covered by a raw file and its minute and hour compactions returns the same partitioned generation, prompt and uncached-prompt totals as the raw file alone, and that after the raw file is removed and the ingest ticks again, the totals are unchanged and come from the minute tier. The live index is not rebuilt or touched by the worker. Gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_telemetry_index.py tests/test_telemetry_ingest.py tests/test_telemetry_compaction_runs.py tests/test_agent_telemetry_watch.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at and each command's exit status is recorded as EXIT=0 or the non-zero status; any evidence fragment written ends with a trailing newline",
